<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 9.106 percent on Monday from 9.274 percent at the previous auction on April 5.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 991.925 million pounds, replace bills worth 992.525 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 900 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):.</p>
<p>Maturity date: Nov 11, 1997 (Nov 4, 1997).</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.106 percent (9.274).</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 991.925 million (978.255 million).</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,977.850 million (2,715.350 million).</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.814-9.239 percent (9.000-9.316).</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.814-10.400 percent (9.000-9.926).</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 178 (107).</p>
<p>Number of bids: 253 (330).</p>
<p>($1 = 3.395 pounds.)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
